{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>And Yitzchak trembled, etc.; moreover, blessed, etc.</b> The reason for two opposite things in one subject: for at first he trembled at the deception, and afterwards he was concerned about what he had already said in his blessing — ״אוֹרְרֶיךָ אָרוּר״ — and he had blessed him. Previously he did not know who it was, and he trembled and was concerned about someone else; but when he reflected on the matter and understood that it was Yaakov who had blessed him — for he detected the scent of his garments and knew the difference between him and Esav — he sealed the blessings. He was also concerned about what he had already said, ״אוֹרְרֶיךָ אָרוּר״; therefore he blessed him."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:43:55.026698132Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}